From: Amir Mazor <mazora@marvell.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: ac5: rd: map the full 4 GiB DRAM window for mmc DMA

On AC5X the DDR is mapped at offset 8 GB (0x2_0000_0000) and the xenon eMMC
controller addresses it with a 34-bit DMA mask (see "mmc: xenon: Add ac5
support via bounce buffer"). On RD boards with more than 2 GB of DRAM the
eMMC enumerates as 0 B and the board never finds its root filesystem.

Add a dma-ranges property to the &mmc_dma node of ac5-98dx35xx-rd.dts that
maps the 4 GiB DRAM window at 0x2_0000_0000 one-to-one for the mmc DMA master.

Signed-off-by: Amir Mazor <mazora@marvell.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/ac5-98dx35xx-rd.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/ac5-98dx35xx-rd.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/ac5-98dx35xx-rd.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/ac5-98dx35xx-rd.dts
@@ -111,3 +111,9 @@
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 };
+
+&mmc_dma {
+        /* Host phy ram DMA mapping */
+        dma-ranges = <0x2 0x0 0x2 0x0000000 0x1 0x0>;
+};
+
